\section{Orders of differentiation}{
Each order of differentiating the predictor through the recursion requires
one more order of the response's family, because the score that drives the
recursion is read at the predictor that the recursion produces. The gradient
reads \eqn{\partial^3 e/\partial u^3} in one direction through
\code{\link[modelterms7:term_third]{modelterms7::term_third()}}. The second derivative of the criterion reads
\eqn{\partial^4 e/\partial u^4} in two directions through
\code{\link[modelterms7:term_fourth]{modelterms7::term_fourth()}}, and the fifth derivative of the family, from
\code{\link[distributions7:distrib_deriv5]{distributions7::distrib_deriv5()}}, enters with it.
}

\section{Form of the assembly}{
The assembly has the form of \code{\link[=statmod_marginal_hess]{statmod_marginal_hess()}}. Write \eqn{u} for
the joint vector, \eqn{K} for the penalized information over it and \eqn{M}
for the matrix against which the trace is taken. Then

\deqn{\frac{\partial^2 V}{\partial t_m\partial t_l}
  = -\rho_{ml} + \hat b_m^\top K \hat b_l
  + \tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}(MK_lMK_m)
  - \tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}\Big(M\frac{\partial K_m}{\partial t_l}\Big),}

where \eqn{\hat b_m = -K^{-1}c_m} is the mode's movement,
\eqn{K_m = S_m + \partial K/\partial u[\hat b_m]}, and the last trace
contains the penalty's second derivative, the twice-contracted second
derivative of \eqn{K} and the once-contracted one at the second movement of
the mode. Every piece is the one that the coefficient-space assembly uses,
read on the joint vector.
}

\section{Blocks that move with their coefficients}{
A block that moves with its coefficients (\code{nl()}, \code{seg()}) beside the filter
